2 5 annotation enrichment of sequence cl:
We provide an option for joint analysis of sequence clustering and annotation information. Users can place annotation terms (Gene Ontology, protein family, etc.) in the definition lines of input FASTA files. For each annotation term A and each cluster C, we use the following numbers: NAC = number of sequences with A in C; NC = number of sequences in C;NAI = number of sequences with A in the input; NI = number of the input sequences.
NAC = number of sequences with A in C;
NC = number of sequences in C;
NAI = number of sequences with A in the input;
NI = number of the input sequences.
A P-value is calculated using the one-tailed Fisher's exact test to assess whether NAC/NC > NAI/NI and annotation term A is enriched in cluster C. Such functionality is very useful to check the cluster quality at different identity levels and also for function assignment of proteins with unknown function.
